# Dev Container: .devcontainer/devcontainer-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored — the resolved
# Feature versions and digests are tracked, so the same commit yields the same environment until
# the lock is refreshed on purpose (ADR-0002, AGENTS.md, section 6).

# Build artifacts
/dist/
/build/
/target/

# Local runtime state (default paths of server.toml / supervisor.toml).
#
# Deliberately *not* anchored to the repository root: these are relative defaults, so they are
# created under whatever directory the process runs in — and `cargo test` runs a crate's unit tests
# with its package directory as the working directory, which puts `crates/fleet-agent/client-state/` in
# the tree. Anchored patterns left those untracked and waiting to be committed by accident.
# The Server's data directory holds the package artifacts too — programs of hundreds of megabytes
# each; they belong in a store, never in the repository (ADR-0026, ADR-0037).
fleet-data/
client-state/

# Environment files — never tracked, in any directory (they may hold secrets);
# a secrets-free .env.example stays tracked
.env*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Per-user agent settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Session artifacts — plans, handoff notes, scratch files (AGENTS.md, section 4)
.scratch/

# Development certificates from scripts/dev-pki.sh — throwaway keys, never committed.
.dev-pki/
